LESSONS = [
L("Chapter 1 — Accounts Settings: the finance constitution", "13", "<p>The fourth and final structural module opens where its three siblings did: the settings screen, read as a constitution — every default a policy the whole finance layer will enforce silently, thousands of times, forever. The walk, field by consequential field, with the accountant and the owner in the room:</p><ul><li><b>Frozen entries and the frozen-edit role</b> — the period lock's configuration (module 7's freeze, Inventory 8's lockstep): the frozen date's advance ritualised, the narrow door's role named to two people, and the setting's health checked exactly as before — a frozen date that never advances is theatre; a broadly-granted edit role is a lock with keys under the mat.</li><li><b>Credit control settings</b> — the credit-limit machinery's master switches (the selling track's gates, configured here): who may override, whether blocked documents hold or warn — the gate numbers' constitutional home.</li><li><b>Payment and allocation settings</b> — the automatic-allocation behaviours, the unlink-on-cancel disciplines (whether cancelling a payment quietly unlinks its allocations — a setting whose wrong value manufactures module 4's unallocated archaeology on its own), and the exchange handling for firms trading in more than naira (gain/loss accounts wired, revaluation governed — the accountant's policy, the system's homes).</li><li><b>Deferred accounting automation</b> — where the machinery spreads deferred revenue and expense by schedule (module 2's matching, automated): enabled deliberately, its accounts wired, its schedules reviewed as the templates they are.</li><li><b>Precision, rounding, and the round-off home</b> — currency precision consistent everywhere (a precision mismatch between documents and ledgers manufactures kobo-level reconciliation noise forever), and the round-off account pointed at its sensible home (module 1's verification hour caught HealthTrade's — the setting this line remembers).</li><li><b>Naming series for financial documents</b> — invoices, payments, journals: series chosen once with the decade view (the registrar's law, final appearance), because the document numbers on a filed VAT return should still make sense to an auditor in year seven.</li></ul><p><b>The walk's discipline, final statement.</b> Each field read as the policy question it is; the answers recorded in the implementation file; the annual re-walk on the calendar; and the corridor toggle convicted one last time in its finance clothes: the setting that keeps obstructing honest work is retuned in the walk, with the accountant, deliberately — never flipped in the hallway to make one afternoon easier, because the hallway flip repeals the constitution for everyone to answer one letter. Four tracks have now taught this in four vocabularies; the consultant who holds it holds the academy's deepest single habit.</p>"),
L("Chapter 2 — Fiscal years & the multi-company frontier", "13", "<p>Two structural facts of the finance layer that the other tracks never needed: time is partitioned into fiscal years, and firms sometimes multiply into companies. The mechanics of both, at the altitude a consultant needs.</p><p><b>Fiscal years.</b> The system partitions financial time into fiscal years — created ahead (the new year existing before its first document needs it: the January 1st invoice that cannot post because nobody created the year is the implementation's most avoidable emergency), aligned to the firm's statutory year (the calendar year for most Nigerian companies, but the system serves any twelve months — the accountant confirms), and closed in sequence (module 7's closing entry per year, the period-closing voucher's governed motion). The fiscal year is also the budget's container (module 6), the comparative reports' axis (this year against last — the trend reads all stand on clean year boundaries), and the reason backdating across a year boundary is the doctrine's most eventful case: an entry into a CLOSED fiscal year moves audited, filed, distributed numbers — the accountant's formal reopening decision at its most formal, and mostly the answer is module 2's rule: correct in the current period, remarks naming the original date.</p><p><b>The multi-company frontier.</b> Firms grow into structures — the trading company and the property company, the Nigerian entity and the planned foreign one, the operating firm and the family holding — and the system's multi-company machinery serves them: each company its own chart (or a shared template, per-company accounts), its own fiscal calendar, its own books sealed separately... inside one system where group-level users see across. The consultant's frame for WHEN this is right: multi-company follows LEGAL reality — separate registered entities keep separate books because the law says they are separate persons (the audit, the tax filing, the liability wall all per entity) — and never convenience (the branch is a dimension, module 6's whole argument; the branch promoted to a company because someone wanted 'separate books' has bought statutory filing obligations to solve a reporting problem a lens would have solved free).</p><p><b>The inter-company discipline, briefly.</b> Where entities genuinely transact — the holding charges management fees, the trading company rents the property company's warehouse, stock moves between sister entities — the movements are REAL third-party-shaped transactions in both sets of books (the sale here is the purchase there; Inventory 5's warning made flesh: inter-company stock movement is a sale and a purchase wearing transfer clothes, priced by a policy the accountant owns because the tax authorities read related-party pricing with professional interest), reconciled between the entities on a rhythm (the inter-company balances agreeing across both books — one more tie, with two ledgers instead of a ledger and its parties), and documented with the discipline related-party scrutiny deserves. The consolidation question — the group's combined statements — is the accountant's terrain with the system's group reports as raw material; the consultant's deliverable is books per entity clean enough that consolidation is arithmetic instead of archaeology. The frontier's one-sentence rule: <b>companies multiply by law, dimensions multiply by reading — and confusing the two costs in both directions.</b></p>"),
L("Chapter 3 — The four finance authorities", "14", "<p>Every structural module of this academy separated its layer's powers; finance's separation is the oldest in the discipline and the one auditors test first. The four authorities, the design, and the matrix.</p><p><b>The four powers.</b> Across seven modules, four distinct authorities have moved the finance layer's truth: <b>RECORD</b> — creating the documents and journals that write the ledger (the trading desks' documents broadly; the journal's pen narrowly — module 2's two names); <b>RELEASE</b> — moving actual money (the payment run's authoriser, the bank mandate's signatories — module 3's preparer-never-releaser); <b>CLOSE</b> — sealing and unsealing time (the freeze's advance, the frozen-edit role, the fiscal year's closing — modules 7 and this one's Chapter 1); and <b>CONFIGURE</b> — the constitution itself (settings, the chart, dimensions, templates — the narrowest of all). Each is a different kind of trust, and the design law is the academy's oldest: <b>the authorities check each other only if they are separated</b> — the recorder whose entries someone else's release pays, the releaser whose payments someone else's reconciliation witnesses, the closer whose seal someone else's audit reads, and nobody's routine role rewriting the constitution.</p><p><b>The classic pairings that must not collapse.</b> The specific separations audits test, each one a module's conviction restated as a permission: the journal pen and the payment release in different hands (the person who can write any entry AND move any money is the fraud triangle's opportunity leg fully assembled); the payment preparer and releaser split (module 3 — two people at any size); the reconciler not the sole releaser (the mover of money not its only checker); the adjust-analogues held narrow (the write-off's two names — module 4; the reconciliation permission's GL twin — module 2's pen); and the frozen-edit role disjoint from the daily recorders (the person posting today should not casually repost yesterday's sealed truth). The sizing honesty, final edition: eleven people means hats share heads — the founder releases what the accountant prepares, the accountant closes what the founder's review witnesses — but the irreducible pairs survive every org chart because they are two PEOPLE, not two departments, and the firm too small for two people in finance is exactly the firm where the owner IS the second pair of eyes, structurally and on the calendar.</p><p><b>The permission matrix as deliverable.</b> The design conversation (who should hold what, and why) encoded as the role matrix — and the closing principle from every structural module, stated for finance where it matters most: <b>permissions enforce a design; they never substitute for one.</b> A finance permission setup nobody can explain is a design nobody made, and the matrix's annual review (people changed; did the design keep up?) sits beside the mandate review (module 3) as the same question asked of the system and the bank. The everything-role — the single user holding record, release, close, and configure because setup was easier that way — is Chapter 9's gravest pattern, and the audit walk-through's first finding every time it exists.</p>"),
L("Chapter 4 — The finance calendar: every rhythm, one page", "13", "<p>Seven modules installed rhythms; the consolidation is the operating system — the academy's fourth and final calendar, and the page the whole finance function runs on.</p><p><b>Daily.</b> The cash position glance (module 3's treasury read — balances, reconciled recency, the day's obligations); the exceptions scan (blocked documents, failed payments, the till sessions' variances flagged overnight); and the entry-hygiene pulse at the desks (references captured, addresses cascading — the disciplines that make every later ritual cheap).</p><p><b>Weekly.</b> The bank items sweep (statement lines arrived, charges to book from the witness, deposits matched); the unallocated glance (module 4's read at its light cadence — items caught young allocate in minutes); and the payment run's cycle where the firm runs one (prepared, evidenced, released by the separated hands).</p><p><b>Monthly — the anchor.</b> The close checklist (module 7's nine lines — the month's spine, days one to five), CONTAINING the subsidiary rituals as its collected inputs: the AR/AP ritual (module 4's ninety minutes), the tax cycles (module 5's six steps per custody, the zeroing verified), the journal audit (module 2's five questions), the bank reconciliations (module 3, every account), the dimension lump sweep (module 6), and the statements read with the MD (modules 7's twenty minutes — the calendar's most important meeting). Plus the branch P&amp;Ls pushed (module 6) and the budget variance read (module 6's six lines).</p><p><b>Quarterly.</b> The provision deep review (the matrix's judgments revisited — module 4); the correction log read by cause (module 2 — the upstream diseases surfaced); the bank charges reasonableness read (module 3); the allocation pool audit (module 6 — direct-first shrinking it); the advance agings' escalations resolved (module 4); and the inter-company reconciliations where the frontier exists (Chapter 2).</p><p><b>Annually.</b> The constitutional season, scheduled ACROSS weeks: the settings walk (Chapter 1), the chart walk (module 1 — every line explainable in one sentence), the dimension audit (module 6), the permission matrix and mandate reviews (Chapter 3, module 3), the capitalisation policy and asset verification (module 7), the budget build (module 6's November), the compliance calendar's re-confirmation against current law (module 5), the fiscal year's closing entry — and the audit season met from twelve folders (module 7).</p><p><b>The page's law, final saying.</b> A rhythm without a name is a hope; the deliverable is this page WITH the names, sized to the firm, reviewed when people change. Four tracks have said it and the fourth saying closes the set: <b>the calendar with owners IS the implementation</b> — the software is its instrument, the policies are its sheet music, and the names are the orchestra. The consultant who leaves all three has finished; the one who leaves only the first has tuned an instrument nobody will play.</p>"),
L("Chapter 5 — The finance handover test", "13", "<p>The academy's deepest thread, at its final surfacing — and finance, the function most often locked in one trusted accountant's head, needs it most of all. The test, the path, and the documentation set.</p><p><b>The test, finance edition.</b> Could a competent newcomer, given what exists, run the finance function for a month with ZERO questions answerable only by the person who left? The walk, module by module: the CHART tells them the language and every account's one-sentence purpose (1); the JOURNAL governance tells them the pen's rules, the recurring set runs itself from templates, and the correction doctrine is written (2); the BANK layer tells them every account, mode, and mandate, with last month's reconciliations showing exactly where each residue stands (3); the AR/AP ritual's checklist and policy pages tell them the tie, the matrix, and the write-off path (4); the COMPLIANCE calendar tells them every obligation, day, authority, and evidence folder — with twelve months of folders showing the pattern (5); the DIMENSION design tells them every address and the allocation policy answers every sharing question by pointing (6); the CLOSE checklist tells them the month's spine in nine ordered lines, and the statement-reading script tells them the MD conversation's shape (7); and THIS module's calendar, matrix, and settings record hold the structure while they learn. Every NO in the walk is a module incompletely done — the test is the audit, and the audit is the goal.</p><p><b>The accountant's path.</b> The handover test read from the other side, one last time: the bookkeeper (entries and hygiene — the desks' disciplines) grows into the ACCOUNTANT (the close's owner, the pen's holder, the statements' first reader) grows into the CONTROLLER (the calendar's owner, the policies' custodian, the MD conversation's co-chair) — and the structured function makes the ladder legible exactly as every track promised: the clean closes, the young residues, the tied bridges are a promotion case written in numbers, while the unstructured function promotes whoever the owner trusts, which caps everyone including the owner. The founder-as-finance-department — this academy's oldest named disease, in its costliest organ — is cured the same way at the fourth telling as at the first: not by finding a hero, but by building the structure a competent professional can hold, and the three-week absence test is its examination.</p><p><b>The documentation set.</b> Every artifact the test walks is a BY-PRODUCT of the modules done properly — the implementation record and settings walks (1, Ch. 1), the policy pages (thresholds, the matrix, the allocation basis, the capitalisation policy — every written number seven modules demanded), the template library with its stories (2), the reconciliation files (3), the ritual checklists with owners (4-7), the compliance folders (5), the close bundles (7), and the calendar with names (Ch. 4). Nothing on the list was created FOR handover; the system that runs well and the system that hands over well are the same system — the academy's quiet thesis, at its final and most consequential organ: the firm whose FINANCE survives its finance person has solved the problem most Nigerian SMEs never do, and the consultant who builds that is selling something no feature list can name.</p>"),
L("Chapter 6 — Internal controls, assembled", "13", "<p>Seven modules built controls one at a time; assembled, they are a SYSTEM — and this chapter is the map: what each control prevents or detects, how they interlock, and the self-assessment that keeps the map current.</p><p><b>The two families.</b> Every control this track installed belongs to one of two families, and knowing which is knowing its job: <b>PREVENTIVE</b> controls stop the error or the fraud before it posts — the separations (the four authorities, the two-names patterns), the validations (mandatory parties, mandatory dimensions, the balance law), the fences (the forbidden journal list, the frozen periods, masters-not-messages), and the gates (approval thresholds, the release separation); <b>DETECTIVE</b> controls catch what slipped through — the reconciliations (the bank, the mirror), the ties (controls-to-parties, the bridges, the zeroing invariant), the audits (the journal audit, the trial-balance scan, the adjustments read), and the reads (the residue agings, the correction log, the unallocated list). The design insight the assembly reveals: the families PAIR — every preventive fence has a detective partner watching its gaps (the journal governance prevented; the journal audit detects; the release separation prevented; the reconciliation detects) — and a control map with unpaired fences is a map with blind spots.</p><p><b>The fraud triangle, briefly and usefully.</b> The classic frame, held at working altitude: fraud needs OPPORTUNITY (the access and the absent control), PRESSURE (the personal circumstance nobody sees), and RATIONALISATION (the story the person tells themselves) — and of the three, the firm controls only opportunity, which is exactly what this track's preventive family shrinks: the everything-role dismantled, the custody segregated, the pen narrowed, the masters guarded. The detective family then shortens the RUNWAY — the fraud that would compound for years surfaces at the month's reconciliation — and the cultural layer this academy has taught throughout (the protections framing: counts protect the honest custodian, signed inspections protect the honest inspector, documented runs protect the honest driver) removes rationalisation's easiest story, because a system that visibly protects the honest is harder to tell yourself is unfair. Three legs, three answers, one system.</p><p><b>The control self-assessment.</b> The map is kept current by the annual CSA — the calendar's constitutional season carrying one more walk: each control on the map confirmed OPERATING (not just designed — the reconciliation that stopped being performed, the second signature that became a rubber stamp, the audit line that quietly dropped off the checklist are all designed-but-dead, and dead controls are worse than absent ones because they manufacture false assurance: the freeze-theatre conviction, generalised). The method is the academy's: evidence, not assertion — last quarter's reconciliation files opened, a sample of large journals checked for their second signature, the residue agings read for museum pieces — an afternoon, annually, and the map stays a map of reality. The consultant's framing for owners closes the chapter: controls are not distrust of people; they are the structure that makes trust AFFORDABLE — the firm with real controls can hire, delegate, and grow on evidence, while the firm without them can only extend trust as far as one person's eyesight, which is the founder-bottleneck wearing its risk costume.</p>"),
L("Chapter 7 — The professional ecosystem: consultant, accountant, auditor", "13", "<p>The finance layer is the one organ the consultant never runs alone — the accountant owns it, the auditor examines it, the tax adviser steers its edges — and the closing craft chapter is the ecosystem's choreography: who owns what, and how the professionals mesh.</p><p><b>The boundary map, consolidated.</b> Four tracks drew it in pieces; assembled: the CONSULTANT owns the MACHINERY — configuration, templates, registers, rituals installed, evidence structured, and the literacy to walk any entry with any professional as a peer (module 1's grammar chapter existing precisely for this); the ACCOUNTANT owns the POLICY — the method choices, the provision matrices, the capitalisation thresholds, the recognition schedules, the reopening decisions, and the statements' professional responsibility; the TAX ADVISER owns the POSITIONS — rates, eligibility, reliefs, and the stances taken where law is unclear (module 5's boundary, at its ecosystem home); and the AUDITOR owns the OPINION — independent, sampled, and served best by being served evidence (module 7's file). The consultant's professional identity in one sentence, worth memorising because clients will blur it monthly: <b>I build and maintain the machine that makes your professionals' judgments executable and evidenced — I do not make their judgments.</b></p><p><b>The collaboration patterns.</b> The meshes that make implementations succeed: the accountant CO-DESIGNS from day one (the chart walk, the posting-map verification, the policy pages — every module's case study had them in the room, which was the point: an accounting layer built FOR an accountant who arrives later is a layer built twice); disagreements between the system's discipline and the accountant's habit resolve by respect-and-evidence (the journal-habit conversation of module 2 — the fluency transferred, never derided); the auditor is MET, not endured (the interim walk-through invited early, the file's structure shared, the adjustments booked by doctrine — the audit relationship compounding across years exactly as the authority relationship does); and the tax adviser is LOOPED at the edges (the new revenue stream's VAT treatment, the related-party pricing, the reform's eligibility questions — brought in BEFORE the configuration, because reconfiguring after a wrong position is the expensive sequence).</p><p><b>The consultant's own protection.</b> The boundary is also armour, stated plainly at the certification's close: the consultant who computes a client's tax, sets their provision, or reprices their stock has assumed a professional liability they are neither qualified for nor insured against — and the discipline of framing findings, quantifying impacts, and handing decisions to the professional who owns them is simultaneously the ethical posture, the legal protection, and — the point four tracks of case studies have made — the TRUST engine: the consultant whose boundaries are clean is the one whose findings get believed, whose recommendations get funded, and whose phone rings when the next firm's books stop making sense. The professional who commands the machinery and honours the boundaries is what this certification certifies — and the final case study shows what that professional can now do.</p>"),
L("Chapter 8 — Case study: the structural year — and the four-track graduate", "16", "<p>The final case study of the final foundation track, in two acts: HealthTrade's finance becomes structure, and the academy's complete graduate walks one last distressed firm.</p><p><b>Act one — the structural year.</b> <b>Q1, the constitution (Ch. 1-2):</b> the settings walk with the accountant — frozen entries ritualised with the two-name door, the unlink-on-cancel setting corrected (it had been quietly manufacturing unallocated archaeology), naming series confirmed for the decade, the next fiscal year created two months early (the January 1st emergency, pre-empted). <b>Q2, the matrix (Ch. 3):</b> the permission review finds the implementation-era everything-role still live on one user — the accountant, holding record, release, close, and configure 'temporarily' since go-live. Dismantled by design conversation, not accusation: the pen and the release split (the founder releases what the accountant prepares — the two hats the firm's size allows, separated correctly), the frozen-edit door confirmed at two names, the matrix documented — and the next audit's walk-through passes its separation tests for the first time. <b>Q3, the CSA (Ch. 6):</b> the first control self-assessment finds one designed-but-dead control — the second signature on large journals, live in the workflow, rubber-stamped in practice (approved in seconds, unread) — revived by the evidence habit: the approver samples one journal's references before signing, the approval time read quarterly. <b>Q4, the absence test (Ch. 5):</b> the founder's three weeks — the trading functions passed last year, the warehouse the year before; this year FINANCE runs on its calendar: the close lands day five without the founder's review (the accountant's graduation), the payment runs release by the deputy-mandate design, the compliance calendar's two filings land on their days, and the handover walk afterwards scores its first clean sheet: zero founder-only questions, in the function where every Nigerian SME keeps the most. The MD's note in the year file: <i>the firm now runs on its documents in every organ — including the one that counts them.</i></p><p><b>Act two — the four-track graduate.</b> A consultant holding all four certifications takes the call every consultant eventually gets: <i>our numbers make no sense — can you look?</i> The books walk, one day, every symptom naming its module: a chart of 400 accounts with per-branch copies (A1, A6), eleven hundred journals a year and idle trading modules (A2 — the machine declined), three banks with one reconciliation eighteen months old and a 'reconciliation differences' account absorbing plugs (A3 — the forged witness), controls diverged from parties since a blob migration (A4 — the tie born broken), custody accounts that never zero and a certificate envelope (A5), one profit and many opinions (A6), no month closed since the fiscal year opened (A7), and one user holding everything (A8). Then the graduate does what four tracks built them to do: reads the WHOLE firm — because the books' diseases have trading-floor causes (the revenue journals trace to invoices never raised at the counter — the selling track's gates absent; the RNB mountain traces to receipts bypassed at the gate — the procurement track's fork absent; the stock figure nobody believes traces to negative stock and selling-price openings — the inventory track's laws absent) — and the findings deck writes itself ACROSS the academy: four tracks, one firm, one remediation sequenced by the curriculum that diagnosed it, priced in phases the prospect can fund, and delivered by running the academy forward. That consultant — able to walk a Nigerian trading firm from the supplier's master record to the branch tailgate to the closed month's statements, and leave every organ structurally better — is what 32 modules, four certifications, and one repeated conviction exist to produce. Take the assessment; then go read a business.</p>"),
L("Chapter 9 — Patterns, the eighth law & the foundation complete", "14", "<p>The structural layer's final scar tissue, the law that closes the track — and the academy's foundation, sealed.</p><p><b>Pattern 1 — the corridor toggle, finance edition.</b> Symptom: frozen dates that never advance; unlink settings flipped per complaint; precision changed mid-year. Disease: the constitution edited casually (Ch. 1). Fix: settings behind the narrowest door, the annual walk as the only editing room — the fourth vocabulary's telling of the academy's deepest habit.</p><p><b>Pattern 2 — the everything-role.</b> Symptom: one user holding record, release, close, and configure; the audit walk-through's first finding, every time. Disease: setup convenience calcified into the fraud triangle's opportunity leg fully assembled (Ch. 3). Fix: the four authorities separated by the two-people patterns, the matrix documented and annually reviewed — and the dismantling run as design conversation, not accusation.</p><p><b>Pattern 3 — the branch promoted to a company.</b> Symptom: statutory filings multiplying; inter-company tangles nobody reconciles; 'separate books' that a dimension would have given free. Disease: the frontier's rule violated (Ch. 2) — companies multiplied by convenience instead of law. Fix: dimensions for reading, companies for legal persons, the wrongly-created entity wound down or made real with the accountant — and the rule taught before the registration fee is spent.</p><p><b>Pattern 4 — designed-but-dead controls.</b> Symptom: reconciliations that stopped; second signatures in seconds; checklist lines quietly dropped. Disease: false assurance manufactured (Ch. 6) — worse than absence, because someone believes the map. Fix: the annual CSA on evidence, approval-time and residue-age reads, and dead controls revived or honestly retired.</p><p><b>Pattern 5 — the hero accountant.</b> Symptom: finance running entirely in one trusted head; leave never taken; the close that only one person can perform; the owner who cannot read the statements without the interpreter present. Disease: the founder-bottleneck's finance twin (Ch. 5) — competence without structure, which is a single point of failure wearing a compliment. Fix: the handover test as the audit, the documentation set as the by-product, the path (bookkeeper → accountant → controller) that makes structure a promotion engine — and the absence test run deliberately before circumstance runs it cruelly.</p><p><b>Pattern 6 — the unowned calendar.</b> Symptom: rhythms that ran while the consultant watched and stopped when they left. Disease: the page without names (Ch. 4) — the implementation's second half never delivered. Fix: the calendar with owners as the closing deliverable, the follow-up visit that checks rhythms not software — the academy's final saying of its oldest sentence.</p><p><b>The eighth law.</b> The chart is the language; the journal is the exception; the bank is the outside witness; the controls tie; tax accounts are custody; profit has an address; the close is a ritual and the statements its testimony. The eighth closes the track as three siblings closed theirs, because it is the same truth in its fourth and final vocabulary: <b>finance that lives in structure — a constitution walked annually, four authorities separated, a calendar with names, controls that pair and operate, and a function that survives its people — is finance that can be trusted, audited, delegated, and grown; finance that lives in a hero survives exactly as long as the hero stays.</b></p><p><b>The foundation, complete.</b> Eight modules: the language (1), the pen (2), the witness (3), the promises (4), the custody (5), the address (6), the testimony (7), the structure (8). And with it the academy's foundation closes at FOUR tracks: <b>Selling</b> (money in), <b>Procurement</b> (money out), <b>Inventory Management</b> (the goods both move), <b>Accounts</b> (the ledger that counts all three) — 32 modules, 32 laws, four continuous case studies through one firm's growth, and one conviction taught in every vocabulary the trade owns: <b>documents over memory, masters over improvisation, rhythms over heroics, structure over trust.</b> The professional who holds all four can walk into any trading firm in Nigeria — its counter, its gate, its warehouse, its books — and read it, price it, repair it, and leave it able to run without them. That is the certification. Take the assessment; then go build one.</p>"),
]

